Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
22.3 The Standard Model plasma on the brane: g*(T), g*s(T) and the \
time\[Dash]temperature relation\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f6b65c47-6999-1d4a-aa18-e2f405fb7124"],

Cell["\<\
With b static the brane obeys the Friedmann equations of section 20.3, 3 M_Pl\
\.b2 Ha\.b2 = \[Rho]_4 + M_Pl\.b2 \[CapitalLambda]4 and Ha\[Prime] = \
\[Minus](\[Rho]_4 + p_4)/(2M_Pl\.b2). In the radiation era \[Rho]_4 = (\[Pi]\
\.b2/30) g*(T) T\:2074 and the entropy s = (2\[Pi]\.b2/45) g*s(T) T\.b3 is \
conserved, s a\.b3 = constant, so that\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3a516a41-a047-7142-8915-565efabdf051"],

Cell["\<\
      Ha = (\[Pi]\.b2 g*/90)^(1/2) T\.b2/M_Pl,     ln a = \[Minus]ln T \
\[Minus] (1/3) ln g*s(T) + const,     t(T) = t(T1) + \[Integral] d(ln a)/Ha = \
t(T1) + \[Integral]_T^T1 (dT\[Prime]/T\[Prime]) [1 + (1/3) d ln g*s/d ln T\
\[Prime]]/Ha(T\[Prime]),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"32048225-a37d-0040-8f66-db43c5271213"],

Cell["\<\
evaluated on 481 points equally spaced in ln T from T1 = 10 GeV (where t(T1) \
= 1/(2Ha)) to 10 keV; on each step 1/Ha is taken exponential in ln T (exact \
when g* is constant), so a step adds \[CapitalDelta](ln a) (1/H_(i+1) \
\[Minus] 1/H_i)/ln(H_i/H_(i+1)); halving the grid changes t by less than 10\
\:207b\:2075.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69d42b31-de3c-a346-a6cb-0ccaf654dd55"],

Cell["\<\
g* and g*s are computed here for ideal gases of all Standard Model particles \
with their masses (PDG values of section 17), with the series for each \
species i (x = m_i/T; +: bosons, \[Minus]: fermions with alternating signs):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"654b915a-2b31-5446-9028-2d41baccb161"],

Cell["\<\
      \[Rho]_i = (g_i T\:2074/(2\[Pi]\.b2)) \
\[CapitalSigma]_{n\[GreaterEqual]1} (\[PlusMinus]1)^(n+1) [3(nx)\.b2 K_2(nx) \
+ (nx)\.b3 K_1(nx)]/n\:2074,   p_i = (g_i T\:2074/(2\[Pi]\.b2)) \
\[CapitalSigma]_{n\[GreaterEqual]1} (\[PlusMinus]1)^(n+1) (nx)\.b2 K_2(nx)/n\
\:2074,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"45c5e1fb-d3c0-034b-8fe5-0eee0559f6b0"],

Cell["\<\
s_i = (\[Rho]_i + p_i)/T. The QCD crossover is modelled by the switch S(T) = \
(1 + tanh((T \[Minus] 0.160 GeV)/0.030 GeV))/2 between quarks and gluons and \
the lightest hadrons (\[Pi], K, \[Eta], \[Rho], \[Omega], K*, \[Eta]\[Prime], \
nucleons); this model differs from the lattice equation of state by up to \
about 10% near the crossover. The neutrinos decouple while e\[PlusMinus] are \
relativistic: T_\[Nu] = T (g_\[Gamma]e(T)/(11/2))^(1/3), and their density is \
scaled by N_eff/3 = 3.044/3. (The Python check tools/ref_coupled.py \
integrates the momentum integrals instead of summing the series.)\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"92e989a1-39bc-6c47-a645-3206cbfd7eb2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
rIIsp = {{2, 0., -1, \"always\"}, {6, 80.3692, -1, \"always\"}, {3, 91.1880, \
-1, \"always\"}, {1, 125.20, -1, \"always\"}, {4, 0.51099895 10^-3, 1, \
\"always\"},
   {4, 0.1056583755, 1, \"always\"}, {4, 1.77693, 1, \"always\"}, {6, 0., 1, \
\"nu\"}, {16, 0., -1, \"qgp\"}, {12, 2.16 10^-3, 1, \"qgp\"}, {12, 4.70 \
10^-3, 1, \"qgp\"},
   {12, 93.5 10^-3, 1, \"qgp\"}, {12, 1.2730, 1, \"qgp\"}, {12, 4.183, 1, \
\"qgp\"}, {12, 172.56, 1, \"qgp\"}, {2, 0.13957039, -1, \"hadron\"}, {1, \
0.1349768, -1, \"hadron\"},
   {2, 0.493677, -1, \"hadron\"}, {2, 0.497611, -1, \"hadron\"}, {1, \
0.547862, -1, \"hadron\"}, {9, 0.77526, -1, \"hadron\"}, {3, 0.78266, -1, \
\"hadron\"},
   {12, 0.8955, -1, \"hadron\"}, {1, 0.95778, -1, \"hadron\"}, {4, \
0.93827209, 1, \"hadron\"}, {4, 0.93956542, 1, \"hadron\"}};
rIInn = N[Range[400]];
rIIrs[t_, g_, m_, st_] := Module[{x = m/t, c, k2, k1},
   If[x > 60, Return[{0., 0.}]];
   c = If[st == 1, (-1.)^(rIInn + 1), 1. + 0 rIInn];
   If[x == 0, Return[With[{r = g t^4 6 Total[c/rIInn^4]/(2 Pi^2)}, {r, 4 r/(3 \
t)}]]];
   k2 = BesselK[2, rIInn x]; k1 = BesselK[1, rIInn x];
   With[{r = g t^4 Total[c (3 (rIInn x)^2 k2 + (rIInn x)^3 k1)/rIInn^4]/(2 \
Pi^2), p = g t^4 Total[c (rIInn x)^2 k2/rIInn^4]/(2 Pi^2)}, {r, (r + p)/t}]];
rIIS[t_] := (1 + Tanh[(t - 0.160)/0.030])/2;
rIIgge[t_] := (rIIrs[t, 2, 0., -1][[2]] + rIIrs[t, 4, 0.51099895 10^-3, \
1][[2]]) 45/(2 Pi^2 t^3);
rIIgstars[t_?NumericQ] := Module[{tot = {0., 0.}, tn, w},
   Do[Which[sp[[4]] == \"nu\", tn = t Min[1, (rIIgge[t]/5.5)^(1/3)]; tot += \
3.044/3 rIIrs[tn, sp[[1]], 0., 1],
      True, w = Switch[sp[[4]], \"qgp\", rIIS[t], \"hadron\", 1 - rIIS[t], _, \
1]; tot += w rIIrs[t, sp[[1]], sp[[2]], sp[[3]]]], {sp, rIIsp}];
   {tot[[1]] 30/(Pi^2 t^4), tot[[2]] 45/(2 Pi^2 t^3)}];
rIIgtab = rIIgstars /@ {1000., 10., 1., 0.3, 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 10.^-4, 10.^-6};
check[\"g* limits: 106.75 above the electroweak scale (to 0.1), 10.75 near 3 \
MeV (to 0.1), 2 + (21/4)(4/11)^(4/3)(3.044/3) = 3.3855 after e+e- \
annihilation (to 10^-3)\",
  Abs[rIIgtab[[1, 1]] - 106.75] < 0.1 && Abs[rIIgstars[0.003][[1]] - 10.75] < \
0.1 && Abs[rIIgtab[[9, 1]] - (2 + 21/4 (4/11)^(4/3) 3.044/3)] < 10^-3]
rIIlnT = Table[Log[10.] - i (Log[10.] - Log[10.^-5])/480, {i, 0, 480}];
rIIgg = rIIgstars[Exp[#]] & /@ rIIlnT;
rIIHg = MapThread[Sqrt[Pi^2 #2[[1]]/90] Exp[2 #1]/rIIMPl &, {rIIlnT, rIIgg}];
rIIlna = -rIIlnT - Log[rIIgg[[All, 2]]]/3;
rIItg = Join[{0.}, Accumulate[Differences[rIIlna] (1/Rest[rIIHg] - \
1/Most[rIIHg])/Log[Most[rIIHg]/Rest[rIIHg]]]] + 1/(2 rIIHg[[1]]);   (* 1/Ha \
exponential in ln T on each step *)
rIIidx[t_] := Round[(Log[10.] - Log[t])/((Log[10.] - Log[10.^-5])/480)] + 1;
rIItvals = rIItg[[rIIidx[#]]] & /@ {1., 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, 10.^-4, 10.^-5};
rIItgHalf = With[{la = rIIlna[[1 ;; -1 ;; 2]], hg = rIIHg[[1 ;; -1 ;; 2]]}, \
Join[{0.}, Accumulate[Differences[la] (1/Rest[hg] - \
1/Most[hg])/Log[Most[hg]/Rest[hg]]]] + 1/(2 hg[[1]])];
check[\"the time-temperature quadrature is converged: halving the grid \
changes t(10 keV) by less than 10^-5\", Abs[Last[rIItgHalf]/Last[rIItg] - 1] \
< 10^-5]
check[\"radiation era: t(1 MeV) = 0.74 s within 5% (1/(2 Ha) with g* = 10.75)\
\", Abs[rIItvals[[4]] rIIhbar/0.74 - 1] < 0.05]
{\"g*, g*s at 1 TeV, 10 GeV, 1 GeV, 300 MeV, 100 MeV, 10 MeV, 1 MeV, 100 keV, \
1 keV\" -> rIIgtab, \"t(T) in s at 1 GeV, 100 MeV, 10 MeV, 1 MeV, 100 keV, 10 \
keV\" -> rIItvals rIIhbar,
 \"1/(2 Ha(T)) / t(T)\" -> (1/(2 rIIHg[[rIIidx[#]]]) & /@ {1., 0.1, 0.01, \
0.001, 10.^-4, 10.^-5})/rIItvals}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1052]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9cb74621-a368-544e-b2a8-e34cab15f777"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"g* limits: 106.75 above the electroweak scale (to 0.1), 10.75 \
near 3 MeV (to 0.1), 2 + (21/4)(4/11)^(4/3)(3.044/3) = 3.3855 after e+e- \
annihilation (to 10^-3)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
