Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24. dirac16complex as dark matter and dark energy", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a980c4ce-700d-f34e-be5b-20a83722c347"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["About section 24. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Section 24 was appended on 27 October 2026. The notebook as it was before \
(sections 0\[Dash]23, with the summary of all checks numbered 24; evaluated) \
is kept in the workspace as backups/7+1_2026-10-27_before_dark.nb (excluded \
from the repository by .gitignore)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d188074-7ea4-f54e-84ce-2b65f118fcbc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The question. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Can the field dirac16complex be the dark matter of the universe, and can it \
be the dark energy? This section answers on the basis of the accurate \
approximate solutions of sections 21\[Dash]23 (the three gravity regimes), \
the couplings of sections 8 and 15\[Dash]20, and present observational data. \
Every statement is marked DERIVED (an exact consequence of the field \
equations of the model, checked below), ESTIMATE (an order-of-magnitude \
statement whose assumptions are stated), or OPEN (not decided by the model). \
Physical parameters as in section 22: M8 = 10 TeV (\[Kappa] = 8\[Pi]G8 = M8\
\:207b\:2076), reduced M_Pl = 2.435 \[Times] 10\.b9\:2078 GeV, V\[UpTee] = \
M_Pl\.b2/M8\:2076, m_r = 10 GeV; the mass m of dirac16complex is free. \
Coordinates as everywhere: x0 time (the octonion unit), x1, x2, x3 ordinary \
space, x4 \[Ellipsis] x7 auxiliary space; \[Eta]17 = diag(+1, \[Minus]1, \
\[Ellipsis], \[Minus]1) is simply the squares of the octonion basis, and xAct \
declares the spacetime with the signature list {7, 1, 0} (seven space-like \
and one time-like dimension)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0d78d5a-aa73-ee45-b81e-4c7d85702398"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24.1 What the observations require", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2ec59e12-db13-0048-968a-3f75d3f331cf"],

Cell["\<\
Data used (as reported by the collaborations; the confidence levels are \
theirs):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"897ac5d1-612b-d243-a14a-4a5b5694ce61"],

Cell["\<\
Planck 2018 (Astron. Astrophys. 641 (2020) A6): \[CapitalOmega]_c h\.b2 = \
0.120 \[PlusMinus] 0.001, \[CapitalOmega]_b h\.b2 = 0.0224 \[PlusMinus] \
0.0001, H0 = 67.4 \[PlusMinus] 0.5 km/s/Mpc, \[CapitalOmega]_m = 0.315 \
\[PlusMinus] 0.007.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4c138fc7-09a0-f044-a948-5a770474f604"],

Cell["\<\
DESI DR2 (DESI Collaboration, arXiv:2503.14738): the evolving dark energy \
w(a) = w0 + wa (1 \[Minus] a) with w0 > \[Minus]1, wa < 0 is preferred over a \
cosmological constant at 3.1\[Sigma] (DESI BAO + CMB) and at 2.8\[Sigma] to \
4.2\[Sigma] when supernovae are added; with Planck PR4 + ACT DR6 + DES-Y5 \
supernovae, w0 = \[Minus]0.753 \[PlusMinus] 0.056, wa = \[Minus]0.84 (+0.23, \
\[Minus]0.20), 4.2\[Sigma] (Garcia-Quintero et al., arXiv:2504.18464).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5710ee80-e791-e043-aa27-3d4597814416"],

Cell["\<\
LZ, 4.2 tonne-years (LZ Collaboration, arXiv:2410.17036): spin-independent \
WIMP\[Dash]nucleon cross section below 2.2 \[Times] 10\:207b\:2074\:2078 cm\
\.b2 at 40 GeV (90% CL).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"ccb036d1-0f83-4448-9fe7-330686106d8f"],

Cell["\<\
Bullet Cluster (Randall et al., ApJ 679 (2008) 1173): self-interaction cross \
section per mass \[Sigma]/m < 1.25 cm\.b2/g (68% CL), < 0.7 cm\.b2/g with \
equal mass-to-light ratios.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"033972bc-e9a3-8342-96a8-c91233a2bf1d"],

Cell["\<\
Lyman-\[Alpha] forest (Ir\[SHacek]i\[CHacek] et al., Phys. Rev. D 109 (2024) \
043511): the mass of a thermal-relic warm dark-matter particle exceeds 5.7 \
keV (95% CL). Dark matter produced by decays of particles in equilibrium is \
warmer than a thermal relic of the same mass and its bound is higher (about 7 \
keV where the thermal-relic bound is 3 keV: Ballesteros, Garcia and Pierre, \
JCAP 03 (2021) 101).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7c29869d-1843-234c-8ecb-47b7f7b259c5"],

Cell["\<\
Pauli principle in dwarf spheroidal galaxies (Alvey et al., MNRAS 501 (2021) \
1188): a fermion with g = 2 internal states is heavier than 0.13 keV (95% \
CL); the bound scales as g^(\[Minus]1/4).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"89b4063a-f1b3-1f41-92ca-b8fecc7a1684"],

Cell["\<\
X-ray lines (NuSTAR, Roach et al., Phys. Rev. D 107 (2023) 023009): limits on \
the mixing of sterile neutrinos of 6\[Dash]40 keV with the active ones, from \
the line of \[Nu]_s \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\[Gamma].\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9220c81f-3f6f-2444-a7e9-861120804122"],

Cell["\<\
Large extra dimensions (Particle Data Group 2024): with M_Pl\.b2 = R^n \
M_D^(n+2) and V = (2\[Pi]R)^n, colliders exclude M_D below 5.9 to 11.2 TeV \
for n = 6 to 2 (ATLAS, 139 fb\:207b\.b9).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f75ae1af-46e2-2b4c-826a-566ab7e5e947"],

Cell["\<\
The dark matter must have the comoving abundance Y = n/s with\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0b598d2f-eb33-4343-bfe5-bb8c46c55780"],

Cell["\<\
      m Y = \[CapitalOmega]_c h\.b2 (\[Rho]_c/h\.b2)/s0,   \[Rho]_c/h\.b2 = 3 \
(100 km/s/Mpc)\.b2 M_Pl\.b2,   s0 = (2\[Pi]\.b2/45) g*s0 T_CMB\.b3,   g*s0 = \
2 + (21/4)(4/11),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a3fcf4d-07d6-ca42-bb6a-bfd63417ae3c"],

Cell["\<\
and in the convention of the Particle Data Group the 7+1 model has M_D = (2\
\[Pi])^(4/6) M8 (V\[UpTee] = (2\[Pi]R)\:2074, M_Pl\.b2 = V\[UpTee] M8\:2076 = \
R\:2074 M_D\:2076). The lightest Kaluza\[Dash]Klein level of dirac16complex \
is four brane Dirac spinors (section 18), i.e. g = 16 internal states (two \
spin states, particle and antiparticle, four spinors): its Pauli bound is \
0.13 keV \[Times] (2/16)^(1/4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"566e10a9-48e5-ec43-82c1-c7550968ad16"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
dkOch2 = 0.120; dkh = 0.674; dkOc = dkOch2/dkh^2; dkHbarC = 1.973269804*^-14; \
         (* hbar c in GeV cm *)
dkRhoc = 3 (100./rIImpc rIIhbar)^2 rIIMPl^2/dkHbarC^3;                        \
           (* rho_c/h^2 in GeV/cm^3 *)
dkGs0 = 2 + 21/4 (4/11); dks0 = 2 Pi^2/45 dkGs0 rIITcmb^3/dkHbarC^3;          \
          (* entropy density today, 1/cm^3 *)
dkYm = dkOch2 dkRhoc/dks0;                                                    \
           (* m Y in GeV *)
dkMD = (2 Pi)^(2/3) rIIM8; dkPauli = 0.13 (2/16)^(1/4);                       \
           (* GeV; keV *)
check[\"required abundance: m Y = Omega_c h^2 (rho_c/h^2)/s0 = 4.37 10^-10 \
GeV with rho_c/h^2 = 1.053 10^-5 GeV/cm^3 and s0 = 2891 cm^-3 (to 10^-3)\",
  Abs[dkRhoc/1.0534*^-5 - 1] < 10^-3 && Abs[dks0/2891.2 - 1] < 10^-3 && \
Abs[dkYm/4.372*^-10 - 1] < 10^-3]
check[\"collider bound: with M_Pl^2 = R^n M_D^(n+2) and V_perp = (2 Pi R)^4 = \
M_Pl^2/M8^6, M_D = (2 Pi)^(2/3) M8 = 34 TeV, above the strongest bound 11.2 \
TeV\",
  Simplify[((2 Pi)^(2/3) m8S)^6 rRS^4 - m8S^6 (2 Pi rRS)^4] === 0 && dkMD > \
11.2*^3]
{\"Omega_c, rho_c/h^2 (GeV/cm^3), s0 (1/cm^3), m Y (GeV)\" -> {dkOc, dkRhoc, \
dks0, dkYm}, \"M_D (GeV)\" -> dkMD,
 \"Pauli bound for g = 16 internal states (keV)\" -> dkPauli}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1110]:=",ExpressionUUID->"15306720-97f8-8248-9448-b23d5cb0adc8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"required abundance: m Y = Omega_c h^2 (rho_c/h^2)/s0 = 4.37 \
10^-10 GeV with rho_c/h^2 = 1.053 10^-5 GeV/cm^3 and s0 = 2891 cm^-3 (to \
10^-3)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535457077`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1115]=",ExpressionUUID->"9bb0cb42-fdfb-e947-831f-5efd78a05f30"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"collider bound: with M_Pl^2 = R^n M_D^(n+2) and V_perp = (2 Pi \
R)^4 = M_Pl^2/M8^6, M_D = (2 Pi)^(2/3) M8 = 34 TeV, above the strongest bound \
11.2 TeV\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535480137`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1116]=",ExpressionUUID->"eb07aa29-b460-6d4e-8d84-a9ee49a614a9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"Omega_c, rho_c/h^2 (GeV/cm^3), s0 (1/cm^3), m Y (GeV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "0.264156592027754`", ",", "0.000010533924943202556`", ",", 
      "2891.284401443723`", ",", "4.372005025009336`*^-10"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"M_D (GeV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "34050.219214767545`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Pauli bound for g = 16 internal states (keV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "0.07729846247517687`"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535500107`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1117]=",ExpressionUUID->"fd7d28d6-559d-984f-8f53-18d770cac9ec"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
24.2 dirac16complex as cold matter in the solutions of sections 21\[Dash]23 \
(DERIVED)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"276019d0-26f5-0744-9e6c-658eb939cac2"],

Cell["\<\
A massive dirac16complex particle with comoving momenta k_a (ordinary space) \
and k_b (auxiliary space) has the comoving energy \[Omega] = (m\.b2 + \
k_a\.b2/a\.b2 + k_b\.b2/b\.b2)^(1/2); the stress tensor of section 20.2 (W = \
\[Omega]) gives \[Epsilon]V = \[Omega], p_a V = k_a\.b2/(3a\.b2\[Omega]), p_b \
V = k_b\.b2/(4b\.b2\[Omega]), with V = a\.b3b\:2074. The lightest mode has \
k_b = 0; once k_a/a \[LessLess] m it is pressureless matter, \[Epsilon] \
\[Proportional] a\:207b\.b3 at fixed b. Every other Kaluza\[Dash]Klein level \
is matter of mass (m\.b2 + k_b\.b2/b0\.b2)^(1/2) with a static pressure p_b \
along the auxiliary space. Consequences in the three regimes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9184fe61-cf07-d043-a26d-397dac775e33"],

Cell["\<\
Regime I: a bulk gas of dirac16complex dominates near x0 = 0 (a \
\[Proportional] \[Tau]^(3/4), section 21.3) and, without the stabilizing \
potential, decompactifies the auxiliary space (\[Tau]Hb \[RightArrow] 2/5 in \
the gas-dominated Einstein regime). dirac16complex as dark matter therefore \
REQUIRES the stabilizer of section 22.1.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b2e6911b-dffa-0f46-925b-bfe935673907"],

Cell["\<\
Regime II: after the capture of the auxiliary space the frozen auxiliary \
momenta are Kaluza\[Dash]Klein masses and the gas is four-dimensional matter, \
its share of the energy constant (section 22.1). Matter of this kind is \
exactly the term \[CapitalOmega]_c a\:207b\.b3 of the late-universe solution \
of section 22.4, so dirac16complex CAN BE the \[CapitalOmega]_c of that \
solution without changing it. Through the radion equation of section 20.3 (\
\[Kappa](\[Epsilon]/6 \[Minus] p_a/2 + p_b/3) with p_a = p_b = 0) it \
displaces the radion by \[Delta]\[Beta] = \[Kappa]\[Epsilon]/(6 m_r\.b2) = H0\
\.b2 \[CapitalOmega]_c/(2 m_r\.b2) (\[Kappa]\[Epsilon] = \[Rho]_DM/M_Pl\.b2 = \
3H0\.b2\[CapitalOmega]_c): G4 = G8/V\[UpTee] does not change.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"32dbd92e-1743-964d-9387-1c0a463d7836"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Regime III: with a(t) = \
(\[CapitalOmega]_m/\[CapitalOmega]_\[CapitalLambda])^(1/3) sinh^(2/3)(3H\
\[Infinity]t/2) (section 23.1), \[Rho]_DM/\[Rho]_\[CapitalLambda] = \
\[CapitalOmega]_c a\:207b\.b3/\[CapitalOmega]_\[CapitalLambda] = (\
\[CapitalOmega]_c/\[CapitalOmega]_m)/sinh\.b2(3H\[Infinity]t/2) \[RightArrow] \
4 (\[CapitalOmega]_c/\[CapitalOmega]_m) e^(\[Minus]3H\[Infinity]t): the dark \
matter, like all matter, dilutes away.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5e8937e0-7d77-ee4c-9aa7-a7305079de95"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
dkSt = feStress[Function[{aa, rIIIbb}, Sqrt[mDM^2 + kaP^2/aa^2 + \
kbP^2/rIIIbb^2]]];
check[\"a massive dirac16complex particle: eps V == omega, pa V == k_a^2/(3 \
a^2 omega), pb V == k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega), omega = Sqrt[m^2 + k_a^2/a^2 + \
k_b^2/b^2]\",
  With[{om = Sqrt[mDM^2 + kaP^2/aS^2 + kbP^2/bS^2]}, Simplify[dkSt aS^3 bS^4 \
- {om, kaP^2/(3 aS^2 om), kbP^2/(4 bS^2 om)}, aS > 0 && bS > 0 && mDM > 0] \
=== {0, 0, 0}]]
check[\"the lightest mode (k_b = 0) is cold matter: pa/eps == k_a^2/(3 (m^2 \
a^2 + k_a^2)) -> 0, pb == 0, and eps ~ a^-3 at fixed b for k_a = 0\",
  Simplify[(dkSt[[2]]/dkSt[[1]] /. kbP -> 0) - kaP^2/(3 (mDM^2 aS^2 + \
kaP^2)), aS > 0 && mDM > 0] === 0 && (dkSt[[3]] /. kbP -> 0) === 0 &&
  Simplify[aS D[Log[dkSt[[1]] /. {kaP -> 0, kbP -> 0}], aS], aS > 0 && mDM > \
0] === -3]
dkDbeta = rIIH0g^2 dkOc/(2 100.);
check[\"dark matter displaces the radion today by H0^2 Omega_c/(2 m_r^2) < \
10^-80 (m_r = 10 GeV): the four-dimensional Newton constant is constant\",
  dkDbeta < 10^-80]
check[\"regime III: Omega_m a^-3/Omega_Lambda == Csch[3 H t/2]^2 for a = \
(Omega_m/Omega_Lambda)^(1/3) Sinh[3 H t/2]^(2/3), and -> 4 Exp[-3 H t]\",
  Simplify[(omS/olS)/((omS/olS)^(1/3) Sinh[3/2 hS tS]^(2/3))^3 - Csch[3/2 hS \
tS]^2, omS > 0 && olS > 0 && hS > 0 && tS > 0] === 0 &&
  Limit[Csch[zS]^2 Exp[2 zS], zS -> Infinity] == 4]
{\"radion displacement by dark matter today\" -> dkDbeta, \"gas share after \
capture (section 22.1) at tau = 10^5, 3 10^5\" -> rIIfrVals,
 \"without stabilizer (section 21.3): tau Hb at Ha = 10^-14\" -> rIlate[\"tau\
\"] rIlate[\"Hb\"]}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1118]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b7542798-783b-5e44-97e6-30e6e8d9ddb5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"a massive dirac16complex particle: eps V == omega, pa V == \
k_a^2/(3 a^2 omega), pb V == k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega), omega = Sqrt[m^2 + \
k_a^2/a^2 + k_b^2/b^2]\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353571005*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1119]=",ExpressionUUID->"67fde906-f8d4-6f4d-b434-0dad6ff37ad1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"the lightest mode (k_b = 0) is cold matter: pa/eps == k_a^2/(3 \
(m^2 a^2 + k_a^2)) -> 0, pb == 0, and eps ~ a^-3 at fixed b for k_a = 0\"\>", 
  "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353571005*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1120]=",ExpressionUUID->"1f6cfe60-edda-3c42-b674-0e9465ec3d3c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"dark matter displaces the radion today by H0^2 Omega_c/(2 \
m_r^2) < 10^-80 (m_r = 10 GeV): the four-dimensional Newton constant is \
constant\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353575451*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1122]=",ExpressionUUID->"5800c6d1-634d-d14d-890e-7cf5cf4ace39"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"regime III: Omega_m a^-3/Omega_Lambda == Csch[3 H t/2]^2 for a \
= (Omega_m/Omega_Lambda)^(1/3) Sinh[3 H t/2]^(2/3), and -> 4 Exp[-3 H t]\"\>",
   "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353582695*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1123]=",ExpressionUUID->"489f8c37-43a6-bd43-97d5-b93d6a586ff4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"radion displacement by dark matter today\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "2.730119736367084`*^-87"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"gas share after capture (section 22.1) at tau = 10^5, 3 \
10^5\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.00859579280101702`", ",", "0.008728032079244996`"}], "}"}]}], 
   ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"without stabilizer (section 21.3): tau Hb at Ha = 10^-14\"\>",
     "\[Rule]", "0.3999953012732535`"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353582695*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1124]=",ExpressionUUID->"eae51e84-3a54-a541-bb07-fa95ba611bc4"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
24.3 The lightest mode: darkness, collisionlessness and stability (ESTIMATE)\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"647bdc26-697d-3242-9258-4759996f9768"],

Cell["\<\
The lightest mode is constant over the auxiliary torus: \[Psi](x, y) = \
\[Chi](x)/\[Sqrt]V\[UpTee] with canonically normalized four-dimensional \
fields \[Chi] (four brane Dirac spinors, section 18). Every coupling at the \
brane or in the bulk is therefore diluted by the volume. With couplings of \
natural size at the eight-dimensional Planck scale \[LongDash] Higgs portal \
\[Lambda]_P = c_P/M8\:2075, Yukawa portal y = c_y/M8\.b2, vector portal G_P = \
c_V/M8\:2076, self-couplings g_r = c_r/M8\:2076 (mass dimensions \[Minus]5, \
\[Minus]2, \[Minus]6, \[Minus]6) \[LongDash] and V\[UpTee] = \
M_Pl\.b2/M8\:2076 the four-dimensional couplings of \[Chi] are\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f18a0fd4-3527-2b4c-9c4d-e496415d94e3"],

Cell["\<\
      \[Lambda]_eff = \[Lambda]_P/V\[UpTee] = c_P M8/M_Pl\.b2,   y_eff = y/\
\[Sqrt]V\[UpTee] = c_y M8/M_Pl,   G_eff = G_P/V\[UpTee] = c_V/M_Pl\.b2,   G_r \
= g_r/V\[UpTee] = c_r/M_Pl\.b2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b824a8d-d433-1041-a0b8-d9c1c4b0f450"],

Cell["\<\
Direct detection (Higgs exchange; the operator \[Lambda]_eff \[CapitalPhi]\
\[Dagger]\[CapitalPhi] \[Chi]\:0304\[Chi] contains \[Lambda]_eff v h \[Chi]\
\:0304\[Chi], the nucleon couples to h with f_N m_N/v, f_N \[TildeTilde] \
0.30): \[Sigma]_SI = \[Lambda]_eff\.b2 f_N\.b2 m_N\.b2 \[Mu]\.b2/(\[Pi] m_h\
\:2074), \[Mu] = m m_N/(m + m_N). Self-interaction (contact): \[Sigma] = G_r\
\.b2 m\.b2/(4\[Pi]). Stability: through the Yukawa portal \[Chi] mixes with \
the neutrinos by \[Theta] = \[Mu]_P/m, \[Mu]_P = y_eff v/\[Sqrt]2 (the portal \
Dirac mass of section 18.2), and decays like a sterile neutrino:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"89d7d3a1-e66e-9e4e-9ca7-48a4e50dc5b6"],

Cell["\<\
      \[CapitalGamma](\[Chi] \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\[Gamma]) = 9 \[Alpha] \
G_F\.b2 m\:2075 sin\.b22\[Theta]/(1024 \[Pi]\:2074),     \[CapitalGamma](\
\[Chi] \[RightArrow] 3\[Nu]) = G_F\.b2 m\:2075 \[Theta]\.b2/(96 \[Pi]\.b3)    \
 (sin\.b22\[Theta] \[TildeTilde] 4\[Theta]\.b2),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fba3de78-eb3f-cb45-982a-cd0e58fd41f3"],

Cell["\<\
the rates of a Majorana fermion (a Dirac fermion decays half as fast; \
immaterial for these estimates); \[CapitalGamma](\[Chi] \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\
\[Gamma])/\[CapitalGamma](\[Chi] \[RightArrow] 3\[Nu]) = 27\[Alpha]/(8\[Pi]). \
The Higgs and vector portals are bilinear in \[Chi] and cannot make it decay; \
without the Yukawa portal \[Chi] is absolutely stable. A lifetime longer than \
the age of the universe is the minimum requirement; searches for the X-ray \
line of \[Chi] \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\[Gamma] demand far longer lifetimes and \
only strengthen the conclusions of section 24.4.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c326ff6-59e7-1947-b578-1ef8d7422741"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"couplings of the lightest mode: with V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6, \
lambda_P/V_perp == c_P M8/M_Pl^2, y/Sqrt[V_perp] == c_y M8/M_Pl, G_P/V_perp \
== c_V/M_Pl^2, g_r/V_perp == c_r/M_Pl^2\",
  With[{vp = mPlS^2/m8S^6}, Simplify[{(cPS/m8S^5)/vp - cPS m8S/mPlS^2, \
(cyS/m8S^2)/Sqrt[vp] - cyS m8S/mPlS, (cVS/m8S^6)/vp - cVS/mPlS^2,
     (crS/m8S^6)/vp - crS/mPlS^2}, mPlS > 0 && m8S > 0] === {0, 0, 0, 0}]]
dkLam = rIIM8/rIIMPl^2; dkYeff = rIIM8/rIIMPl; dkGr = 1/rIIMPl^2; dkGeV2g = \
1.78266192*^-24;     (* per unit c_P, c_y, c_r; grams per GeV *)
dkSigSI[cpx_, mx_] := With[{mu = mx 0.9383/(mx + 0.9383)}, (cpx dkLam)^2 \
0.30^2 0.9383^2 mu^2/(Pi mHb^4) dkHbarC^2];    (* cm^2 *)
dkSigM[crx_, mx_] := (crx dkGr)^2 mx/(4 Pi) dkHbarC^2/dkGeV2g;                \
                                      (* cm^2/g *)
dkCrMax[mx_] := Sqrt[4 Pi 0.7 dkGeV2g/(dkHbarC^2 mx)]/dkGr;
dkMuP[cyx_] := cyx dkYeff vEW/Sqrt[2];
dkTauG[cyx_, mx_] := rIIhbar/(9/137.035999 gFermi^2 mx^5 4 \
(dkMuP[cyx]/mx)^2/(1024 Pi^4));
dkTau3[cyx_, mx_] := rIIhbar/(gFermi^2 mx^5 (dkMuP[cyx]/mx)^2/(96 Pi^3));
dkAge = rIIage rIIgyr;
dkMmax = (dkTau3[1, 1.]/dkAge)^(1/3);                            (* tau(chi \
-> 3 nu) = tau(m = 1 GeV)/(c_y^2 m^3) *)
check[\"natural couplings make the lightest mode dark and collisionless: \
sigma_SI(c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV) < 10^-50 x (LZ limit 2.2 10^-48 cm^2), \
sigma/m(c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV) < 10^-70 cm^2/g (Bullet Cluster: 0.7 cm^2/g)\",
  dkSigSI[1, 40.] < 10^-50 2.2*^-48 && dkSigM[1, 1.] < 10^-70]
check[\"stability through the Yukawa portal: for c_y = 1 the lifetime chi -> \
3 nu equals the age of the universe at m = 40 MeV; it scales as 1/(c_y^2 \
m^3), and Gamma(nu gamma)/Gamma(3 nu) == 27 alpha/(8 Pi)\",
  0.03 < dkMmax < 0.05 && Abs[dkTau3[1, dkMmax]/dkAge - 1] < 10^-12 && \
Abs[dkTau3[2, 0.01]/dkTau3[1, 0.01] - 1/4] < 10^-12 &&
  Abs[dkTau3[1, 0.02]/dkTau3[1, 0.01] - 1/8] < 10^-12 &&
  Abs[dkTau3[1, 0.01]/dkTauG[1, 0.01] - 27/(8 Pi 137.035999)] < 10^-12]
{\"lambda_eff, y_eff, G_r per unit coupling (GeV^-1, 1, GeV^-2)\" -> {dkLam, \
dkYeff, dkGr}, \"sigma_SI (cm^2) at c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV\" -> dkSigSI[1, 40.],
 \"sigma/m (cm^2/g) at c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV; c_r allowed by the Bullet Cluster \
at m = 1 GeV\" -> {dkSigM[1, 1.], dkCrMax[1.]},
 \"portal mass mu_P (GeV) at c_y = 1; lifetimes chi -> nu gamma, chi -> 3 nu \
(s) at c_y = 1, m = 1 GeV and 10 keV\" -> {dkMuP[1], dkTauG[1, 1.], dkTau3[1, \
1.], dkTauG[1, 10^-5], dkTau3[1, 10^-5]},
 \"largest m (GeV) with lifetime > age for c_y = 1\" -> dkMmax}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1125]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c6286ec1-bf74-ac48-b6e5-f6ad86c62a9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"couplings of the lightest mode: with V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6, \
lambda_P/V_perp == c_P M8/M_Pl^2, y/Sqrt[V_perp] == c_y M8/M_Pl, G_P/V_perp \
== c_V/M_Pl^2, g_r/V_perp == c_r/M_Pl^2\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353582695*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1125]=",ExpressionUUID->"172ffc33-e441-c545-a4ed-b74348ac30c8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"natural couplings make the lightest mode dark and \
collisionless: sigma_SI(c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV) < 10^-50 x (LZ limit 2.2 10^-48 \
cm^2), sigma/m(c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV) < 10^-70 cm^2/g (Bullet Cluster: 0.7 \
cm^2/g)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535944195`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1135]=",ExpressionUUID->"1cb9736f-79f4-1648-8158-2bcf50f3423c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"stability through the Yukawa portal: for c_y = 1 the lifetime \
chi -> 3 nu equals the age of the universe at m = 40 MeV; it scales as \
1/(c_y^2 m^3), and Gamma(nu gamma)/Gamma(3 nu) == 27 alpha/(8 Pi)\"\>", "\[Rule]",
   "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535944195`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1136]=",ExpressionUUID->"070d45ae-6ca7-7843-9746-71978fae4a6a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"lambda_eff, y_eff, G_r per unit coupling (GeV^-1, 1, \
GeV^-2)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "1.68656105983497`*^-33", ",", "4.106776180698152`*^-15", ",", 
      "1.68656105983497`*^-37"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"sigma_SI (cm^2) at c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "9.55607696287784`*^-104"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"sigma/m (cm^2/g) at c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV; c_r allowed by the \
Bullet Cluster at m = 1 GeV\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"4.944225003643582`*^-79", ",", "1.1898710736040751`*^39"}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"portal mass mu_P (GeV) at c_y = 1; lifetimes chi -> nu gamma, \
chi -> 3 nu (s) at c_y = 1, m = 1 GeV and 10 keV\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "7.150044241252334`*^-13", ",", "3.593359688030265`*^15", ",", 
      "2.8170199696474516`*^13", ",", "3.5933596880302647`*^30", ",", 
      "2.817019969647451`*^28"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"largest m (GeV) with lifetime > age for c_y = 1\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "0.040151337853037906`"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147353596426*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1137]=",ExpressionUUID->"3e9a36c1-9160-d649-8fd4-11cb0e8e81fe"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24.4 The abundance (ESTIMATE; the outcome is OPEN)", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bb5e60b1-99c1-d244-8194-4b3f4b704022"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["From the solutions of sections 21\[Dash]22: overproduction. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The minimal model makes far too much dirac16complex, not too little:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a53ad61-43ea-414d-9f7a-1d5b9aa778f7"],

Cell["\<\
The primordial gas (sections 21.3 and 22.1). After capture the gas carries \
the fraction f = 0.0087 of the energy and the radion the rest (for the \
normalization of section 21.3; f scales with it). Even if the radion energy \
all became brane radiation at T_RH, the gas-to-radiation ratio f/(1 \[Minus] \
f) would have to equal \[Rho]_DM/\[Rho]_rad = (4/3) m Y/T_RH (\[Rho]_rad/s = \
3T/4); it exceeds it by O = (f/(1 \[Minus] f)) T_RH/((4/3) m Y) = 1.5 \
\[Times] 10\:2077 (T_RH/GeV), i.e. 6 \[Times] 10\:2074 even for the lowest \
T_RH = 4 MeV allowed by nucleosynthesis.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5b92dbc1-a525-1b49-8b34-a7f64b0989ae"],

Cell["\<\
Radion decay (section 22.2). The radion does NOT become brane radiation: it \
decays 1.3 \[Times] 10\.b9\.b3 times faster into Kaluza\[Dash]Klein pairs of \
dirac16complex (if 2m < m_r) than into brane fields. Without a later dilution \
the universe after the radion decay is made of dirac16complex, with a brane \
share of only \[CapitalGamma]_brane/\[CapitalGamma]_bulk \[TildeTilde] 8 \
\[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\:2074 \[LongDash] the opposite of the observed ratio.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"173f2f98-660a-1d4c-b13e-f037183dc0e7"],

Cell["\<\
Both results mean that dirac16complex as dark matter needs the dilution and \
reheating that the moduli problem already needs (section 22.2), at T_RH below \
the normalcy temperature T* = (M8\:2076/M_Pl)^(1/5) = 13.3 GeV. After it the \
abundance is set by the portals. With instantaneous reheating, production by \
decays of Higgs bosons in equilibrium below T_RH carries the factor\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"db6f66ff-67fe-0a42-b1d5-f0f07662379c"],

Cell["\<\
      S(x) = (2/(3\[Pi])) \[Integral]_x^\[Infinity] t\.b3 K_1(t) dt,   x = \
m_h/T_RH   (S(0) = 1 because \[Integral]_0^\[Infinity] t\.b3 K_1(t) dt = 3\
\[Pi]/2;  S = 0.0078 at T_RH = T*),\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"751bf7d3-0ad5-4947-a5a5-6fc4cb477b97"],

Cell["\<\
and the freeze-in yield of a particle made in h decays with partial width \
\[CapitalGamma] is Y = (135/(8\[Pi]\.b3\[CenterDot]1.66)) \
(M_Pl^(unreduced)/(g*^(3/2) m_h\.b2)) \[CapitalGamma] S (Hall, Jedamzik, \
March-Russell and West, JHEP 03 (2010) 080; M_Pl^(unreduced) = 1.221 \[Times] \
10\.b9\:2079 GeV, g* = 106.75; below the electroweak bosons g* = 86.25, so \
for T_RH < m_W this understates Y by at most (106.75/86.25)^(3/2) = 1.4). \
Production by other processes adds to this; the estimates below are therefore \
lower bounds on what each portal makes, except for the zero mode alone (an \
upper bound up to factors of order one, S = 1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3665d7d9-83ed-204c-b511-104d78d50242"],

Cell["\<\
Yukawa portal, the zero mode. \[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\:0304\
\[Chi]) + \[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] \[Nu]\[Chi]\:0304) = y_eff\.b2 \
m_h/(16\[Pi]) per channel (N channels: three lepton flavours and the brane \
spinors, N \[LessEqual] 12): Y = 9.7 \[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\:2078 c_y\.b2 N S. \
The abundance grows like c_y\.b2 m while the lifetime \[Tau](\[Chi] \
\[RightArrow] 3\[Nu]) = K/(c_y\.b2 m\.b3) falls; both conditions hold \
together only for m < m* = (Y(c_y = 1) K/(m Y t0))^(1/2) = 1.2 keV (N = 1), \
4.2 keV (N = 12), even with S = 1 \[LongDash] below the Lyman-\[Alpha] bound.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1c1a4e30-ba19-564a-a6ca-fb435457ba2d"],

Cell["\<\
Yukawa portal, the Kaluza\[Dash]Klein tower. Every Kaluza\[Dash]Klein level \
couples to the brane with the same strength as the zero mode (section 18.2), \
so the Higgs decays make the whole tower below m_h: the yield is multiplied \
by \[CapitalSigma]_n (1 \[Minus] \[Mu]_n\.b2/m_h\.b2)\.b2 = V\[UpTee] m_h\
\:2074/(192\[Pi]\.b2) = 7.7 \[Times] 10\.b9\:2077 (continuum limit of the \
lattice sum; for the lattice sum with r_4(k) see the check below), with mean \
mass (192/315) m_h = 76 GeV: Y_tower = 7.5 c_y\.b2 N S and a mass per entropy \
571 c_y\.b2 N S GeV. At T_RH = T* the tower carries more energy than all the \
dark matter unless c_y < 9.9 \[Times] 10\:207b\:2076 (N = 1); and through the \
same mixing its states decay into neutrinos and photons long after \
nucleosynthesis (\[Tau](\[Chi]_n \[RightArrow] 3\[Nu]) = 2.8 \[Times] 10\.b9\
\:2070 s/c_y\.b2 at \[Mu]_n = 10 GeV; other channels shorten it by about \
ten). The Yukawa portal must therefore be very weak or absent; the precise \
bound from nucleosynthesis and the CMB is not derived here (OPEN). With c_y < \
10\:207b\:2075 the zero mode lives longer than the universe for m < 86 GeV, \
and its freeze-in yield is negligible.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0e541421-2bf4-914e-8af2-6dc4f98907ab"],

Cell["\<\
Higgs portal. The zero mode gets Y = 2.0 \[Times] 10\:207b\:2074\:2079 \
c_P\.b2 S (\[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] \[Chi]\[Chi]\:0304) = \
(\[Lambda]_eff v)\.b2 m_h/(8\[Pi])). But the brane breaks the conservation of \
Kaluza\[Dash]Klein momentum, so \[Lambda]_eff v h \[Chi]\:0304_n \[Chi]_m \
couples EVERY pair of levels: \[CapitalGamma](h \[RightArrow] \[Chi]_n \[Chi]\
\:0304_m) = (\[Lambda]_eff v)\.b2 m_h (1 \[Minus] (u_n + u_m)\.b2)^(3/2) (1 \
\[Minus] (u_n \[Minus] u_m)\.b2)^(1/2)/(8\[Pi]), u = \[Mu]/m_h. With the \
density of levels dN = V\[UpTee] \[Mu]\.b3 d\[Mu]/(8\[Pi]\.b2) the sum over \
all pairs is (V\[UpTee] m_h\:2074/(8\[Pi]\.b2))\.b2 = 3.4 \[Times] 10\.b3\
\:2078 times I_hp = \[Integral]\[Integral]_(u1+u2<1) u1\.b3 u2\.b3 (1 \
\[Minus] (u1 + u2)\.b2)^(3/2) (1 \[Minus] (u1 \[Minus] u2)\.b2)^(1/2) du1 du2 \
= 9.5 \[Times] 10\:207b\:2075 (with the mass weight u1 + u2 under the \
integral: I_hp^E). For four brane spinors the pairs carry 2.5 \[Times] 10\
\:207b\.b9\.b2 c_P\.b2 S GeV per entropy (mean pair mass I_hp^E/I_hp = 0.77 \
m_h): the observed abundance needs c_P = 13 for T_RH \[GreaterGreater] m_h (S \
\[RightArrow] 1) and c_P = 150 at T_RH = T* \[LongDash] two orders of \
magnitude above natural size; for c_P = 1 it is 4.5 \[Times] 10\:207b\:2075 \
of the dark matter. Such dark matter would be a population of heavy Kaluza\
\[Dash]Klein modes (tens of GeV), whose decays into lighter levels and \
Standard Model particles through the same portal are not computed here (OPEN).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1df3bcb3-4a5f-6c4d-bdfd-afbaf31b5220"],

Cell["\<\
Vector portal (and any coupling of gravitational strength per pair, G_eff = \
c_V/M_Pl\.b2). Summed over the pairs lighter than T the production rate \
divided by H is of order c_V\.b2 (T/T_V)\.b9\.b9 with T_V = \
(M8\.b9\.b2/M_Pl)^(1/11) = 490 GeV (numerical factors omitted; they raise \
T_V): 5 \[Times] 10\:207b\.b9\:2078 at T*. Negligible.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e77c4899-e3cf-2049-8cc4-015c0b5adfb8"],

Cell["\<\
Hence, with couplings of natural size, the minimal model does not produce the \
observed abundance after the dilution its moduli problem requires: the Yukawa \
portal must be tiny, the vector portal is negligible, and the Higgs portal \
falls short by a factor 2 \[Times] 10\:2074 (it would need c_P \[TildeTilde] \
150). The abundance must come from physics outside the minimal model (OPEN).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"055618a4-5420-2849-b7d7-22478124c26d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
dkF = rIIfrVals[[2]]; dkOver[trh_] := (dkF/(1 - dkF)) trh/(4/3 dkYm);
dkFracBulk = rIIgBulk/(rIIgBulk + rIIgam);
check[\"primordial gas: overabundance O = (f/(1 - f)) T_RH/((4/3) m Y) = 1.5 \
10^7 T_RH/GeV (6 10^4 at T_RH = 4 MeV)\",
  Abs[dkOver[1.]/1.51*^7 - 1] < 0.01 && 5*^4 < dkOver[0.004] < 7*^4]
check[\"the radion puts more than 1 - 10^-12 of its decays into the bulk \
(Kaluza-Klein pairs of dirac16complex)\", 1 - dkFracBulk < 10^-12]
{\"gas share after capture f, overabundance O at T_RH = 1 GeV and 4 MeV\" -> \
{dkF, dkOver[1.], dkOver[0.004]}, \"fraction of radion decays into the bulk; \
brane share\" -> {dkFracBulk, rIIgam/rIIgBulk}}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1138]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5215d851-055a-de4b-93f2-6f70e7518efa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"primordial gas: overabundance O = (f/(1 - f)) T_RH/((4/3) m Y) \
= 1.5 10^7 T_RH/GeV (6 10^4 at T_RH = 4 MeV)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
  "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473535984325`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1140]=",ExpressionUUID->"f46d4562-b047-ff47-b554-cb1197fb6228"],

Cell[BoxData[
