Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["24.5 dirac16complex and dark energy", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6c0dc392-97dd-ff43-9901-ed9b150a00bc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Matter cannot be dark energy (DERIVED). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Free particles have p_a = \[Minus]\[PartialD]_aW/(3a\.b2b\:2074) \
\[GreaterEqual] 0 because W decreases with a. The interacting Kohn\[Dash]Sham \
matter of section 8 (units m = 1, gS = \[Minus]10\:2075, gV = 10\:2074) has, \
at zero temperature, p = \[Mu]\[Rho] \[Minus] \[Epsilon] with \[Mu] = \
\[Epsilon]_F (Hugenholtz\[Dash]Van Hove, section 8.7), so p = \[Rho]\.b2 d(\
\[Epsilon]/\[Rho])/d\[Rho]: the pressure is negative only where the energy \
per particle decreases with density \[LongDash] below the saturation density, \
where uniform matter has a higher energy than droplets at saturation in empty \
space (both have p = 0) and is metastable or, in the spinodal region dp/d\
\[Rho] < 0, unstable. Its most negative equation of state there is w = p/\
\[Epsilon] \[TildeTilde] \[Minus]0.058 (at kF \[TildeTilde] 0.67): nowhere \
near \[Minus]1."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c7ac1598-93b2-554c-b813-685ad2c1dfb8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A condensate is only a cosmological constant (DERIVED). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "A Lorentz-invariant condensate of dirac16complex \
(\[LeftAngleBracket]\[Psi]bar \[Psi]\[RightAngleBracket] \[NotEqual] 0, which \
the self-couplings of section 15 allow) has T_\[Mu]\[Nu] \[Proportional] g_\
\[Mu]\[Nu], i.e. w = \[Minus]1 exactly: a contribution to \[CapitalLambda]4, \
not a dynamical dark energy."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a2932d6-ece3-e84f-ba0b-e01db67dcb1b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Vacuum energy is only a contribution to \[CapitalLambda]4 \
(DERIVED, with an ESTIMATE of its size). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "The zero-point energy of dirac16complex on the auxiliary torus (periodic \
boundary conditions) is a Casimir energy. For a field of mass m in eight \
dimensions with four compact directions of proper size ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] = V\[UpTee]^(1/4) the four-dimensional vacuum energy per real \
bosonic degree of freedom is \[Minus](2/",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]\:2074) \[CapitalSigma]_(n \[Element] Z\:2074, n \[NotEqual] 0) (m",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]/(2\[Pi]|n|))\:2074 K_4(m",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]|n|) \[RightArrow] \[Minus]\[CapitalGamma](4) Z/(\[Pi]\:2074 ",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee]\:2074) for m \[RightArrow] 0, with the Epstein sum Z = \
\[CapitalSigma]_(n \[NotEqual] 0) |n|\:207b\:2078 = 8(1 \[Minus] 4\:207b\.b3) \
\[Zeta](4) \[Zeta](3) (from r_4(k) of section 22.2); a fermion contributes \
with the opposite sign, and dirac16complex has 16 real degrees of freedom on \
shell. Massless it gives +6.8 \[Times] 10\.b3\:2074 \[Rho]_\[CapitalLambda]; \
it equals \[Rho]_\[CapitalLambda] only for m",
 StyleBox["\[ScriptL]",
  FontFamily->"Cambria Math"],
 "\[UpTee] = 92.2 (m = 59 MeV), and the graviton (20 degrees of freedom) \
contributes \[Minus]8.5 \[Times] 10\.b3\:2074 \[Rho]_\[CapitalLambda]. Every \
such term is constant while b is frozen (w = \[Minus]1 up to the radion \
displacement, 10\:207b\:2078\:2076), and they add to \[CapitalLambda] + \
\[Kappa]U0 + \[Kappa]f_W/V\[UpTee]: the observed \[CapitalLambda]4 needs \
their sum to cancel to 10\:207b\.b3\:2075 of each \[LongDash] the \
cosmological-constant problem, not solved by dirac16complex."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"161aa0cb-e06b-984c-aedf-8f067fc5577f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The prediction w = \[Minus]1. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "With the radion frozen the model predicts w = \[Minus]1 exactly; the DESI \
preference for w0 > \[Minus]1, wa < 0 (2.8\[Sigma] to 4.2\[Sigma]), if \
confirmed, would contradict it whatever dirac16complex is. (The radion, the \
only scalar of the model, cannot be the dark energy either: with m_r \
\[GreaterGreater] H0 it is frozen; a radion light enough to roll today would \
change G4 = G8 e^(\[Minus]4\[Beta])/V\[UpTee] by order one \[LongDash] \
ESTIMATE.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0bd29828-cc25-f146-85ed-5c48bc7fca2b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
dkPE[kf_?NumericQ] := With[{e = eps7[gS0, gV0, kf]}, {fermi7[gS0, gV0, kf] \
rho7[kf] - e, e}];   (* {p, eps}: p = mu rho - eps with mu = eps_F *)
dkPres[kf_?NumericQ] := dkPE[kf][[1]];
dkWtab = Table[With[{pe = dkPE[kf]}, {kf, pe[[1]], pe[[1]]/pe[[2]]}], {kf, \
5/100, 85/100, 1/100}];
dkWmin = Min[dkWtab[[All, 3]]]; dkKmin = dkWtab[[Ordering[dkWtab[[All, 3]], \
1][[1]], 1]];
check[\"Kohn-Sham matter of section 8: p > 0 at low density, p < 0 below \
saturation, p = 0 at kF0, a spinodal region (dp/dkF < 0) in between, and w = \
p/eps >= -0.06 everywhere\",
  dkWtab[[1, 2]] > 0 && dkPres[N[kF0, 40] - 1/100] < 0 && Abs[dkPres[kF0]] < \
10^-20 && AnyTrue[Differences[dkWtab[[All, 2]]], # < 0 &] && -0.06 < dkWmin < \
-0.04]
dkZ48 = 8 (1 - 4^-3) Zeta[4] Zeta[3];
check[\"Epstein sum over Z^4 without 0: Sum |n|^-8 == 8 (1 - 4^-3) zeta(4) \
zeta(3), compared with the shell sum Sum r_4(k)/k^4 to k = 20000 (tail < 3 \
10^-8)\",
  Abs[N[dkZ48, 20] - Total[rIIr4[[1 ;; 20000]]/N[Range[20000]]^4]] < 3*^-8]
dkLp = rIIVp^(1/4); dkRhoL = 3 rIIH0g^2 rIIMPl^2 rIIOL;
dkC0 = Gamma[4]/Pi^4 dkZ48;                                   (* massless, \
per real degree of freedom, times 1/l^4 *)
dkCas[xx_?NumericQ] := 16 Total[rIIr4[[1 ;; 400]] 2 (xx/(2 Pi \
Sqrt[N[Range[400]]]))^4 BesselK[4, xx Sqrt[N[Range[400]]]]]/dkLp^4;
dkXL = xxV /. FindRoot[Log[dkCas[xxV]/dkRhoL] == 0, {xxV, 90}];
check[\"Casimir energy of dirac16complex on the auxiliary torus: massless 16 \
Gamma(4) Z/(Pi^4 l^4) > 10^34 rho_Lambda, the massive sum -> the massless \
value for m l -> 0 (to 10^-4), and equals rho_Lambda at m l = 92.2\",
  16 dkC0/dkLp^4/dkRhoL > 10^34 && Abs[dkCas[10^-3]/(16 dkC0/dkLp^4) - 1] < \
10^-4 && Abs[dkXL - 92.2] < 0.05]
{\"w_min of Kohn-Sham matter and its kF (units m = 1); saturation kF0\" -> \
{SetPrecision[dkWmin, MachinePrecision], N[dkKmin], N[kF0]}, \"rho_Lambda \
(GeV^4)\" -> dkRhoL,
 \"Casimir energy / rho_Lambda: dirac16complex (m = 0), graviton (20 dof)\" \
-> {16 dkC0/dkLp^4/dkRhoL, -20 dkC0/dkLp^4/dkRhoL},
 \"m l_perp and m (GeV) at which the dirac16complex Casimir energy equals \
rho_Lambda\" -> {dkXL, dkXL/dkLp},
 \"kF, p, w at kF = 0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.6, 0.67, 0.7, 0.75 (units m = 1)\" -> \
N[Select[dkWtab, MemberQ[{1/10, 3/10, 1/2, 3/5, 67/100, 7/10, 3/4}, #[[1]]] \
&]],
 \"dirac16complex Casimir energy / rho_Lambda at m l_perp = 1, 10, 30, 60\" \
-> (dkCas[#]/dkRhoL & /@ {1., 10., 30., 60.})}\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[1168]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e573e847-734d-7c45-8c4c-cf3039393b25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Kohn-Sham matter of section 8: p > 0 at low density, p < 0 \
below saturation, p = 0 at kF0, a spinodal region (dp/dkF < 0) in between, \
and w = p/eps >= -0.06 everywhere\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.002147354943577*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1172]=",ExpressionUUID->"dd2929d3-1a5a-8145-9b7a-fc965a00f1d6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\<\"Epstein sum over Z^4 without 0: Sum |n|^-8 == 8 (1 - 4^-3) \
zeta(4) zeta(3), compared with the shell sum Sum r_4(k)/k^4 to k = 20000 \
(tail < 3 10^-8)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0021473549466133`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1174]=",ExpressionUUID->"d216e0f0-7c83-ca46-9a3a-d7048b5e3752"],

