integer algebraic curvature tensors)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Gauss-Bonnet density in invariant form: L_2 == R^2 - 4 Ric.Ric + \
Riem.Riem (the same tensors, exact)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"stabilizing potential: W = a^3 b^4 U(b) gives eps = U, pa = -U, pb \
= -U - (b/4) U'(b)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane tension smeared over the torus (V_perp = b^4 Lc^4): eps = \
f_W/V_perp, pa = -f_W/V_perp, pb = 0\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane fluid rho_4 = N a^(-3(1+w)), smeared: eps = rho_4/V_perp, pa \
= w eps, pb = 0\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"massless dirac16complex particle (comoving momentum (k_a, k_b)): \
eps V = omega, pa V = k_a^2/(3 a^2 omega), pb V = k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega)\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"every such source is conserved: eps' + 3Ha(eps + pa) + 4Hb(eps + \
pb) == 0 for arbitrary W(a, b), a(x0), b(x0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"minisuperspace: EL_n == (a^3 b^4/kappa)(S00 - kappa eps), EL_a == \
(3 a^2 b^4/kappa)(S11 + kappa pa), EL_b == (4 a^3 b^3/kappa)(S44 + kappa pb) \
with S = Sum alpha_k E^(k) (identities of section 12.6)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion equation of Einstein gravity: Hb' + 3 Ha Hb + 4 Hb^2 == \
kappa (eps/6 - pa/2 + pb/3) + Lambda/3 (constraint used)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion mass: U = U0 + (K_U/2) beta^2, b U' = K_U beta gives the \
restoring term -(kappa K_U/12) beta, m_r^2 = kappa K_U/12\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"static auxiliary space: (kappa/4) b U' == Lambda + kappa U + 2 \
kappa f_W/V_perp + (kappa/2)(eps - 3pa) + kappa pb - 12 alpha2 Ha^2 (Ha' + \
Ha^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"static auxiliary space: Ha' == -(kappa/2)(eps + pa) and E^(3) does \
not contribute (Hb = 0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane Friedmann equation: 3 Ha^2 == (kappa/V_perp) rho_4 + Lambda4 \
with Lambda4 = Lambda + kappa U0 + kappa f_W/V_perp, i.e. 8 Pi G4 = \
kappa/V_perp\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein-frame form of the constraint: 3 (Ha + 2 Hb)^2 == 6 Hb^2 + \
(E^(1)0_0 of section 12.6), i.e. 3 M_Pl^2 H_E^2 == phi'^2/2 + rho with phi = \
Sqrt[12] M_Pl beta\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"vacuum constraint in u = Hb/Ha, X = Ha^2 (alpha2 = 1, alpha3 = xi): \
P_E + X P_G + xi X^2 P_C == 0 with P_E = 3(2u^2 + 4u + 1), P_G = -12u(u^3 + \
12u^2 + 18u + 4), P_C = 360 u^3 (3u + 4)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kasner constants: P_E(u1) == 0, p1 == (1 + 2 Sqrt[2])/7, q1 == (2 - \
3 Sqrt[2])/14; u2 in (-1/3, 0) with P_G(u2) == 0, 3 p2 + 4 q2 == 3\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"the explicit curve solves the vacuum constraint: residual < 10^-25 \
(relative) at u = u1 + 10^-6, -0.28, u2, -0.1, -10^-4 (xi = 10^-6, 40 digits)\
\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the effective exponent along the curve: p_eff -> p1 (u -> u1), \
about p2 at u = u2 (within 10^-2), -> 1 (u -> 0)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic regime: Ha = 1/tau + A0 + A1 tau, Hb = h0 + h1 tau + h2 tau^2 \
solves the 00, 11, 44 equations through order tau^-1 (11: checked, not \
used)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic regime coefficients: h1 == alpha2/(16 alpha3) - 1/(32 \
alpha2), A0 == Sqrt[30](58 alpha2^2 - 45 alpha3)/(1920 alpha2^(3/2) \
alpha3^(1/2)), A1 and h2 as in the text\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein regime: u = u1 + d1 Ha^2, d1 == alpha2 (16 - 11 \
Sqrt[2])/4; p_eff = p1 + e1 Ha^2, e1 == alpha2 (1 + 9 Sqrt[2])/7\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Gauss-Bonnet regime: p_eff = p2 + f1/Ha^2 + f2 xi Ha^2 with f1 = \
-0.69887346..., f2 = -0.7853407... (differences give the same values at Ha = \
10^4 and 10^-6 xi Ha^2 to 10^-5)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"cubic-series data at tau = 10^-8 satisfy the vacuum constraint to < \
10^-12 (relative to 48 Ha^3 |Hb|)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the ODE solution agrees with the exact quadrature: tau at Ha(u2) to \
10^-10, and tau - p1/Ha + e1 Ha at Ha = 3 10^-3 equals s1 to 10^-6\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"regime approximations: cubic error < 10^-5 for Ha >= 10^4, \
Gauss-Bonnet < 10^-3 for 3 <= Ha <= 300, Einstein < 10^-3 for Ha <= 0.1\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"matter-dominated cubic regime: p_eff -> 3/4, Hb -> -Sqrt[alpha2/(54 \
alpha3)], kappa eps tau^3 -> 9 alpha2 |h*|, alpha2 E2 : alpha3 E3 : kappa eps \
-> 9/4 : -5/4 : 1 (Ha = 10^15)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"coupled: where the gas is a small fraction the effective exponents \
are those of the vacuum (1, p2, p1 within 10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"without the stabilizing potential the gas-dominated Einstein regime \
decompactifies: tau Ha -> 0, tau Hb -> 2/5, pb/eps -> 1/4 (Ha = 10^-14)\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"the gas fraction grows like tau^(2 - 3 p1 - 5 q1) = tau^1.160 in \
the Einstein regime (to 2 10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein + fluid power laws a ~ tau^P, b ~ tau^Q: (wa, wb) = (0, \
1/4) -> (0, 2/5); (1/3, 0) -> (1/2, 0); (1/7, 1/7) -> (1/4, 1/4) (tau^2 E^(1) \
from EKas of section 14.1)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"matter-dominated cubic regime (any fluid, b finite): leading 44 \
term p^3 (p - 1)(648 alpha3 h^2 - 12 alpha2); with h^2 = alpha2/(54 alpha3): \
p = 1/(1 + w_a) and kappa eps tau^3 = (64/3) p^3 alpha2 |h|\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Einstein-Kasner pair creation: F(1) == 0.0107493 (section 14.3) and \
the tail F ~ K^(-(3 Sqrt[2] + 2)/2) (exponent between K = 8 and 16 to 2 \
10^-2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"brane plasma at T = M8, H = M8: fraction (Pi^2 g*/30) M8^4/(3 \
M_Pl^2 M8^2) < 10^-27\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"capture: the radion oscillates like a four-dimensional massive \
field in a matter-dominated universe: with tau_E from <H_E> = 2/(3 (tau - \
tau_E)) over the last period, beta = A sin(m_r tau + vartheta)/(m_r (tau - \
tau_E)) to 2 10^-2, <H_E>(tau - tau_E) = 2/3 to 10^-2 at tau = 10^5 and 2 \
10^5, the gas share constant to 2 10^-2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"through brane fields alone a 10 GeV radion would decay far too \
late: T_RH < 10^-6 GeV (nucleosynthesis needs 4 10^-3 GeV); 10^13 \
Kaluza-Klein channels below m_r/2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the number of lattice vectors with |n|^2 = k is r_4(k) = 8 sigma(k) \
- 32 sigma(k/4) (direct count for k <= 60)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion decays into the bulk: the lattice sum over the \
Kaluza-Klein modes of dirac16complex (m << m_r/2) equals its continuum limit \
to 10^-6, the number of momenta to 10^-5, and Gamma_bulk/Gamma_brane > \
10^12\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"g* limits: 106.75 above the electroweak scale (to 0.1), 10.75 near \
3 MeV (to 0.1), 2 + (21/4)(4/11)^(4/3)(3.044/3) = 3.3855 after e+e- \
annihilation (to 10^-3)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the time-temperature quadrature is converged: halving the grid \
changes t(10 keV) by less than 10^-5\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radiation era: t(1 MeV) = 0.74 s within 5% (1/(2 Ha) with g* = \
10.75)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"age of the universe from the brane Friedmann equation: 13.79 Gyr \
(Planck 2018: 13.787 +- 0.020)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"composite analytic solution t(a) = t_rm(a) + t_mLambda(a) - t_m(a) \
accurate to < 3 10^-4 for 10^-8 <= a <= 10^0.5\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"far future: Ha(t) = H_inf Coth[3 H_inf t/2] agrees with the full \
brane solution at a = 3 and a = 10 to 10^-4\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"radion in de Sitter: gamma/(3H) and m_eff^2/m_r^2 as in the text \
(beta_eq -> 0); gamma = 3H and m_eff^2 = m_r^2 for alpha2 = alpha3 = 0\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"radion equilibrium in de Sitter: 3 m_r^2 beta_eq == 3 H^2 - 12 \
alpha2 H^4 + O(beta_eq^2)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion relaxes to the equilibrium of the two algebraic \
equations: beta(3000) to 10^-6, Ha(3000) to 10^-8 (relative)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"eight-dimensional de Sitter (no stabilizer): all three equations \
read 21 H^2 - 420 alpha2 H^4 + 2520 alpha3 H^6 == Lambda\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the shares of the four terms of the 00 equation: Einstein > 0.99 at \
Ha = 10^-2, Gauss-Bonnet > 0.9 at Ha = 30, Gauss-Bonnet and cubic about 1/2 \
each at Ha = 3 10^5, gas > 0.1 at Ha = 10^15\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"required abundance: m Y = Omega_c h^2 (rho_c/h^2)/s0 = 4.37 10^-10 \
GeV with rho_c/h^2 = 1.053 10^-5 GeV/cm^3 and s0 = 2891 cm^-3 (to 10^-3)\"\>",
      "True"},
    {"\<\"collider bound: with M_Pl^2 = R^n M_D^(n+2) and V_perp = (2 Pi R)^4 \
= M_Pl^2/M8^6, M_D = (2 Pi)^(2/3) M8 = 34 TeV, above the strongest bound 11.2 \
TeV\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"a massive dirac16complex particle: eps V == omega, pa V == k_a^2/(3 \
a^2 omega), pb V == k_b^2/(4 b^2 omega), omega = Sqrt[m^2 + k_a^2/a^2 + \
k_b^2/b^2]\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the lightest mode (k_b = 0) is cold matter: pa/eps == k_a^2/(3 (m^2 \
a^2 + k_a^2)) -> 0, pb == 0, and eps ~ a^-3 at fixed b for k_a = 0\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"dark matter displaces the radion today by H0^2 Omega_c/(2 m_r^2) < \
10^-80 (m_r = 10 GeV): the four-dimensional Newton constant is constant\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"regime III: Omega_m a^-3/Omega_Lambda == Csch[3 H t/2]^2 for a = \
(Omega_m/Omega_Lambda)^(1/3) Sinh[3 H t/2]^(2/3), and -> 4 Exp[-3 H t]\"\>", 
     "True"},
    {"\<\"couplings of the lightest mode: with V_perp = M_Pl^2/M8^6, \
lambda_P/V_perp == c_P M8/M_Pl^2, y/Sqrt[V_perp] == c_y M8/M_Pl, G_P/V_perp \
== c_V/M_Pl^2, g_r/V_perp == c_r/M_Pl^2\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"natural couplings make the lightest mode dark and collisionless: \
sigma_SI(c_P = 1, m = 40 GeV) < 10^-50 x (LZ limit 2.2 10^-48 cm^2), \
sigma/m(c_r = 1, m = 1 GeV) < 10^-70 cm^2/g (Bullet Cluster: 0.7 cm^2/g)\"\>",
      "True"},
    {"\<\"stability through the Yukawa portal: for c_y = 1 the lifetime chi \
-> 3 nu equals the age of the universe at m = 40 MeV; it scales as 1/(c_y^2 \
m^3), and Gamma(nu gamma)/Gamma(3 nu) == 27 alpha/(8 Pi)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"primordial gas: overabundance O = (f/(1 - f)) T_RH/((4/3) m Y) = \
1.5 10^7 T_RH/GeV (6 10^4 at T_RH = 4 MeV)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"the radion puts more than 1 - 10^-12 of its decays into the bulk \
(Kaluza-Klein pairs of dirac16complex)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Boltzmann factor of production below T_RH: Int_0^Infinity t^3 \
K_1(t) dt == 3 Pi/2 (exact), S(0) = 1, S(m_h/T*) < 10^-2 with T* = \
(M8^6/M_Pl)^(1/5) = 13.3 GeV\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"zero mode through the Yukawa portal: the abundance (~ c_y^2 m) and \
the stability (lifetime ~ 1/(c_y^2 m^3) > age) are compatible only for m < \
m*, and m* < 5.7 keV (Lyman-alpha) for N = 1 and N = 12 channels even with S \
= 1\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kaluza-Klein tower: Sum_n (1 - mu_n^2/m_h^2)^2 -> V_perp m_h^4/(192 \
Pi^2) and Sum_n mu_n (1 - mu_n^2/m_h^2)^2 -> V_perp m_h^5/(315 Pi^2) (d^4n = \
2 Pi^2 |n|^3 d|n|: exact integrals); the lattice sums with r_4(k) for R = 100 \
equal Pi^2 R^4/12 and 16 Pi^2 R^4/315 to 10^-8\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kaluza-Klein tower through the Yukawa portal: 7.7 10^17 states \
below m_h with mean mass (192/315) m_h; at T_RH = T* it carries more energy \
than all the dark matter unless c_y < 2 10^-5 (N = 1)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Higgs portal: the zero mode gets Y < 10^-40 (c_P = 1); the pairs of \
Kaluza-Klein levels (lambda(1, u1^2, u2^2) == (1 - (u1 + u2)^2)(1 - (u1 - \
u2)^2)) give the observed abundance only for c_P between 10 and 20 (T_RH >> \
m_h, S -> 1) or between 100 and 200 (T_RH = T*)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"vector portal: gravitational strength per pair; the production rate \
of all pairs lighter than T divided by H ~ (T/T_V)^11 with T_V = \
(M8^12/M_Pl)^(1/11) = 490 GeV is below 10^-17 at T*\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Kohn-Sham matter of section 8: p > 0 at low density, p < 0 below \
saturation, p = 0 at kF0, a spinodal region (dp/dkF < 0) in between, and w = \
p/eps >= -0.06 everywhere\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Epstein sum over Z^4 without 0: Sum |n|^-8 == 8 (1 - 4^-3) zeta(4) \
zeta(3), compared with the shell sum Sum r_4(k)/k^4 to k = 20000 (tail < 3 \
10^-8)\"\>", "True"},
    {"\<\"Casimir energy of dirac16complex on the auxiliary torus: massless \
16 Gamma(4) Z/(Pi^4 l^4) > 10^34 rho_Lambda, the massive sum -> the massless \
value for m l -> 0 (to 10^-4), and equals rho_Lambda at m l = 92.2\"\>", 
     "True"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
